@crew pell
// Head writer 4: career lines. Pell nearly left in his first month; he knows the feeling from the inside.
== career.worried
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.missed
- Took your scrubber job this morning. No bother. Just... you all right, {nick}?
? tier>=colleague flag:career.low
- Chief's talk? Had one my first month. Felt like the floor went. It didn't. Go.   #warm
? tier>=friend flag:career.verylow
- I nearly left too, my first month. Glad every day I didn't. Don't you go either.   #serious
? tier>=friend flag:career.bottom
- I'll sleep at night for once. Swear. Then I'll wake you. Shift, tomorrow. Yeah?   #serious
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.up
- Back on the board! The bay sounds right again.
== career.eve
? tier>=friend flag:career.eve
- Tomorrow? Oh, {nick}. I didn't think. I really didn't think it'd go this far.   #serious
== career.bye
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.lastday
- Today, eh. I'll be at the Tern. Bringing you something. Don't guess.   #warm
== career.seeoff
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.lastday
- Every ship I've fixed is in my tin. You're in there now too.   #warm
== career.leave
? flag:leave.booked
- Leave? Nice. Sleep all day. That's what I'd do. That's what I do anyway.   #funny
== career.back
? flag:leave.back
- You're back! I did your rounds. The Deck 5 panel still sticks. Some things never change.
